{
  "rationale": "We separate plant automata for perception (sensing obstacles) and actuation (motion commands). The specification automata bind sensor outcomes to safe, coverage-oriented actions, enforce recovery after obstacles, and prevent unsafe or oscillatory behaviors. Recovery is conservative but brief, with a strong bias to return to forward exploration as soon as possible.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model perception and actuation as separate plants for modularity and clarity.",
    "Specifications enforce safe recovery, single-action-per-state, and rapid return to exploration, with full_rotate reserved for repeated blockage."
  ],
